WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.034 --> 00:00:02.302
-Good evening.
I'm Seth Meyers.

00:00:02.302 --> 00:00:03.336
And this is "Late Night."
We hope you're doing well.

00:00:03.336 --> 00:00:05.204
And now we're going to
get to the news.

00:00:05.204 --> 00:00:07.340
In a living room.

00:00:07.340 --> 00:00:11.310
In an apartment owned
by people I've never met.

00:00:11.310 --> 00:00:12.645
According to a new survey,

00:00:12.645 --> 00:00:15.314
just 9% of Americans said
that the Biden administration

00:00:15.314 --> 00:00:18.684
is doing a great job handling
the Omicron coronavirus strain.

00:00:18.684 --> 00:00:22.788
I assume it's the same 9%
who don't currently have it.

00:00:22.788 --> 00:00:25.058
Oh, you're cocky now.

00:00:25.058 --> 00:00:26.525
But it's coming.

00:00:26.525 --> 00:00:27.927
According to a new poll,

00:00:27.927 --> 00:00:30.529
President Biden's
overall disapproval rating

00:00:30.529 --> 00:00:32.432
hit a new high last month,

00:00:32.432 --> 00:00:36.935
or as his aides are phrasing it,
"Your numbers are way up, sir."

00:00:36.935 --> 00:00:38.904
The CDC is reportedly

00:00:38.904 --> 00:00:41.841
considering updating
its coronavirus guidance

00:00:41.841 --> 00:00:46.780
to recommend that people
wear N95 or KN95 masks

00:00:46.780 --> 00:00:51.317
or, barring that, just 95 masks.

00:00:51.317 --> 00:00:54.921
The CDC also issued a
do-not-travel advisory yesterday

00:00:54.921 --> 00:00:58.057
for Canada due to an increase
in coronavirus cases there,

00:00:58.057 --> 00:01:00.092
which is kind of
like Keith Richards

00:01:00.092 --> 00:01:03.996
telling you not to hang around
with that pothead from school.

00:01:03.996 --> 00:01:05.398
According to new reports,

00:01:05.398 --> 00:01:07.400
Senate Democrats have grown
tired of trying to convince

00:01:07.400 --> 00:01:09.368
West Virginia Senator
Joe Manchin

00:01:09.368 --> 00:01:11.003
to support
a federal elections bill

00:01:11.003 --> 00:01:14.873
and complained that it's "like
negotiating via Etch A Sketch."

00:01:14.873 --> 00:01:19.412
Which begs the question,
have you tried shaking him yet?

00:01:19.412 --> 00:01:22.015
The federal government
has reportedly approved Facebook

00:01:22.015 --> 00:01:24.850
for hundreds of new patents
over the last few months

00:01:24.850 --> 00:01:26.052
for augmented

00:01:26.052 --> 00:01:28.620
and virtual reality technology
they've created.

00:01:28.620 --> 00:01:32.892
It's great for escaping
this hellish actual reality

00:01:32.892 --> 00:01:35.261
which they also created.

00:01:35.261 --> 00:01:40.333
The makers of Goldfish have
unveiled a new type of cracker

00:01:40.333 --> 00:01:42.902
that's 50% bigger
than the original snack

00:01:42.902 --> 00:01:45.204
and specifically made
for adults.

00:01:45.204 --> 00:01:47.640
Please, I'm a grown man.

00:01:47.640 --> 00:01:50.076
I'm not gonna eat Goldfish.

00:01:50.076 --> 00:01:53.278
I just had two string cheeses
and a Fruit Roll-Up,

00:01:53.278 --> 00:01:55.981
and my tummy's a mess.

00:01:55.981 --> 00:01:57.750
According to a new documentary,

00:01:57.750 --> 00:02:00.319
"Playboy" founder
Hugh Hefner's pet poodle

00:02:00.319 --> 00:02:02.188
was addicted to cocaine,

00:02:02.188 --> 00:02:06.292
though according to my eyes,
all of them are.

00:02:06.292 --> 00:02:09.362
That's right, Hugh Hefner's
poodle was addicted to cocaine,

00:02:09.362 --> 00:02:13.232
which explains why he was
so afraid of the vacuum cleaner.

00:02:13.232 --> 00:02:16.669
"No! My stash!"

00:02:16.669 --> 00:02:21.440
Yeah, dogs -- dogs on cocaine
sound like Samberg.

00:02:21.440 --> 00:02:23.909
That's just science.

00:02:23.909 --> 00:02:28.248
And finally, Tesla recently
released a new version

00:02:28.248 --> 00:02:31.918
of its self-driving software
that allows drivers to select

00:02:31.918 --> 00:02:34.620
among three different
aggression profiles,

00:02:34.620 --> 00:02:39.225
including chill, average,
or New Jersey Turnpike.

00:02:39.225 --> 00:02:42.328
And I'm hearing -- Really?

00:02:42.328 --> 00:02:45.665
Was the 1 millionth
monologue joke

00:02:45.665 --> 00:02:49.268
with the punch line
"New Jersey Turnpike."

00:02:49.268 --> 00:02:52.304
Across all talk shows,
since the history of talk shows.

00:02:52.304 --> 00:02:55.207
And is that true?

00:02:55.207 --> 00:02:59.779
I'm gonna get a $10
E-ZPass credit for that.

00:02:59.779 --> 00:03:02.715
So, ha-ha,
things are looking up.

